 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? That's disappointing, but not surprising. Many art venues see hundreds of submissions for each slot, and they get crowded. Sure, send them full set of paintings, with a strong title on each image so they spot them immediately, in an email with a short personalise message. A good story about each piece, maybe where it was painted, or how it came to be, helps too. That's a good choice. Galleries and museums in big cities get hundreds of queries a day, easy to miss something amazing. cafes, on the other hand, often buy work directly off the wall.",
